189 - All That Thrills My Soul
 / 
Key: Bb
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 189
Topic: Jesus Christ - 

Verse 1:
[Bb]Who can cheer the heart like Jesus, [Eb/G]By [F7]His presence all divine?
[Bb]True and tender, pure and precious, Oh, how blest to call Him mine!
[Eb]All that thrills my [F7]soul is Jesus; He is more than life to me; (to [Bb]me;)
[Bb]And the [Adim]fairest [Gm]of ten [Dm]thousand, [Cm]In my blessed Lord I see.

Refrain:
[F]All that thrills my soul is Jesus;
[Bb]He is more than life to me; [Eb](to [Cm]me;)
[F7]And the fairest of ten thousand,
[Bb]In my blessed Lord I see.

Verse 2:
[Bb]Love of Christ so [Eb/G]freely [F7]given,
[Bb]Grace of God beyond degree,
[Eb]Mercy [F7]higher than the heaven,
[Bb]Deeper [Gm]than [Dm]the [Cm]deepest sea.

Verse 3:
[Bb]Every need [Eb/G]His [F7]hand supplying,
[Bb]Every good in Him I see;
[Eb]On His [F7]strength divine relying,
[Bb]He [Adim]is [Gm]All [Dm]in [Cm]All to me.

Verse 4:
[Bb]By the crystal [Eb/G]flowing [F7]river
[Bb]With the ransomed I will sing,
[Eb]And forever [F7]and forever
[Bb]Praise [Adim]and [Gm]glorify [Cm]the King
